+  # SDL 2.32.10 has no visionOS branch where it picks a HIDAPI platform backend
+  # (cmake/sdlchecks.cmake tests `if(IOS OR TVOS)`), so it compiles SDL_hidapi.c
+  # with nothing behind it and the app fails to link on every PLATFORM_hid_*
+  # symbol. HIDAPI is raw USB/Bluetooth device access, which visionOS does not
+  # offer an app in the first place; controllers arrive through GameController,
+  # and SDL's MFi joystick driver — which reads GameController — stays on.
